## About

I finished my Computer Science degree and I'm now doing a Master's in High-Performance Computing. My focus areas are:

- **HPC**
- **Computer Vision**
- **AI**
- **Big Data**

I also build personal projects across different fields of CS, and design is still close to my heart, so I like to take things end to end: from the interface on the screen to the web, mobile and backend pieces behind it.

This repository is the website that tells that story.

## Highlights

| | |
|---|---|
| **Star-map navigation** | A hero built around the Canopus star, with a constellation of sections to explore. |
| **Journey timeline** | Education and experience on a glowing timeline that opens up year by year. |
| **Skill cards** | Seven flip cards, one per skill category. |
| **Certificate dial** | A rotating dial of certificates, each with details of what it covers and why it matters. |
| **GitHub Universe** | Every repository drawn as a planet, loaded live from the GitHub API. The closer to the sun, the fresher the code. |
| **Project showcase** | Project cards with screenshot galleries and demo videos. |
| **Transmission console** | A contact form styled as a deep-space relay. Visitors pick a mission type, write a message, and send it straight to my inbox. |
| **Star portrait** | A profile picture framed by a galaxy star, with a scan reveal, 3D tilt and light sheen on hover. |
| **Smooth and light** | Staggered scroll reveals, inertial wheel scrolling on desktop, animations that pause off screen, and `prefers-reduced-motion` support. |

## Built with

- Plain **HTML, CSS and JavaScript** in a single file, with no frameworks, no build step and no dependencies
- **SVG** for icons and shapes, and **Canvas** for the warp intro and cursor trail
- **GitHub REST API** for the live repository universe
- **[FormSubmit](https://formsubmit.co)** for the contact form (no backend needed)

## Project structure

```
.
├── index.html            # the whole site (rename from portfolio.html)
├── README.md
└── assets/
    ├── logo.png
    ├── profile.png       # transparent star portrait
    ├── certificates/     # one image per certificate
    └── projects/
        ├── erctrack/
        ├── op3/
        ├── hami-ai/
        ├── canopus-realm/
        ├── restaurant/
        ├── gameverse/
        └── fieldops/     # screenshot-1.jpg, screenshot-2.jpg, video-1.mp4 ...
```

## Run it locally

No install needed.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/YOUR-REPO.git
cd YOUR-REPO

# just open index.html in your browser, or serve it:
python3 -m http.server 8000
# then visit http://localhost:8000
```

> The contact form and the GitHub universe need a real `http(s)` address, so use the local server above instead of double-clicking the file.

## Customize

**Project media.** Put files in `assets/projects/<project>/` named `screenshot-1`, `screenshot-2`, ... and `video-1`. Numbers start at 1 with no gaps. `screenshot-1` is the card cover. To change how many screenshots a project has, edit `shots:` or `videos:` in the `PROJECTS` list inside the file.

**Certificates.** Add an image to `assets/certificates/` named after the certificate (for example `ethical-hacking.jpg`). Each certificate's text, skills and optional verify link live in the `CERTS` list.

**Profile picture.** Use a PNG with a transparent background at `assets/profile.png`.

**Contact form.** Messages are sent through FormSubmit. The first message triggers a one-time activation email to the address set at the top of the contact script. Click the link in it once and every message after that arrives normally. To use another service (Web3Forms, Formspree), change the `ENDPOINT` value.

## Deploy with GitHub Pages

1. Rename `portfolio.html` to `index.html`.
2. Push to your repository.
3. Go to **Settings → Pages**, choose your branch (`main`) and the `/ (root)` folder, then save.
4. Your site goes live at `https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/YOUR-REPO/` within a couple of minutes.

